 "difficulty": "Medium",
 "description": "You are given a list `nums` of distinct integers. Return every possible ordering (permutation) of them. The permutations can be listed in any order.\n\n**Constraints**\n\n- `1 <= len(nums) <= 6`",
 "function": "permute",
 "params": [
  "nums"
 ],
 "starter": "class Solution:\n    def permute(self, nums: List[int]) -> List[List[int]]:\n        pass\n",
 "compare": "unordered",
 "hints": [
  "Build each permutation one position at a time, choosing any number that has not been used yet.",
  "Track which numbers are used (a set or a boolean list) as you recurse.",
  "`dfs(path)`: if `len(path) == len(nums)`, record a copy. Otherwise, for each unused number, mark it used, append it, recurse, then undo both."
